    long: "The integers extend the [[natural-number|natural numbers]] so that subtraction always works: $3 - 5 = -2$ is an integer. They are closed under addition, subtraction and multiplication, but not division, since $7 \\div 2$ is not an integer.\n\nOn the [[number-line|number line]] the integers are evenly spaced points with no gaps between consecutive ones. Every integer $n$ is also a [[rational-number|rational number]], because $n = \\tfrac{n}{1}$.\n\nPitfall in code: integer division throws away the fractional part. In C++, `7 / 2` is `3` and `-7 / 2` is `-3` (truncation toward zero), while mathematically $7 \\div 2 = 3.5$. Write `7.0 / 2` when you want the real quotient.",
