    long: "You can add or multiply in any order and get the same result. This is what lets you rearrange $3 + x + 5$ into $x + 8$, or write $x \\cdot 4$ as $4x$.\n\nSubtraction and division are *not* commutative: $5 - 2 \\ne 2 - 5$ and $6 \\div 3 \\ne 3 \\div 6$. Rewriting subtraction as adding a negative, $a - b = a + (-b)$, restores commutativity so you can reorder terms safely.\n\nLater you will meet operations that are not commutative even though they look like multiplication: [[composition|composition of functions]] ($f \\circ g \\ne g \\circ f$ in general) and [[matrix|matrix]] multiplication. Rotations in a 3D game are the same story: rotating then translating differs from translating then rotating.",
